   "text": {
    "L1": "Light travels in straight lines. A shadow forms when an opaque object blocks those lines.",
    "L2": "A shadow is not a reflection. It is the dark region behind the object where light cannot reach.",
    "L3": "To see a shadow, we need a light source, an opaque object, and a screen such as a wall or the ground.",
    "L4": "The torch sends straight rays toward the wall, but the ball stops the rays in its path.",
    "L5": "The shadow shows the object's outline, but it does not show its colour or details.",
    "L6": "Move the object closer to the torch, and it blocks a wider cone of light. Its shadow becomes bigger.",
    "L7": "Near the wall, the object blocks a narrower cone, so the shadow is about its own size.",
    "L8": "Turn the object, and the shape of its shadow can change. Now check the idea."
   },
